    "description": "Held on 12 June 1993 under a two-party system in which the military government had created only the SDP and NRC; voting used the open-ballot 'Option A4' method, with the SDP's Moshood Abiola defeating the NRC's Bashir Tofa by roughly 58% to 42%. Observers judged the poll free and fair, but before final results could be formally released the regime of General Ibrahim Babangida annulled the election on 24 June 1993. State-level figures below are the collated unofficial results leaked by democracy activists, since the result was never officially declared."
